  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "5pb7X3GpoCA5Lq7vPKiSR87oafM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:29.786Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The storyline is compressed into four beats: get structured data from your documents; tag a document as an invoice; \"But how much money was spent?\"; use the structured data for analytics and for workflow automation.\n\nThe third beat is the hinge. Tagging is where document-management tools stop \u2014 the document is classified and findable. The question of how much was spent cannot be answered from a tag, only from the fields inside the document, and it is a question every viewer already knows they need answered.\n\nThe pattern generalises beyond Paperless: find the question the incumbent's abstraction cannot express, and ask it out loud. It is the same construction as the tool-screen demos, which turn on destroying a record and then asking who approved it.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:29.786387Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:29.786392Z"
    }
  },
